Python Starters, video 9.

3
00:00:05.959 --> 00:00:07.890
Make it readable.

4
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.020
Readable code is kinder to future you — and to teachers reviewing your work.

5
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.548
Use clear variable names.

6
00:00:17.598 --> 00:00:21.055
Add one comment describing the purpose.

7
00:00:21.105 --> 00:00:23.573
Keep consistent indentation.

8
00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.900
End with a final print of the result.

9
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.344
Teachers can follow your thinking.

10
00:00:31.394 --> 00:00:34.118
You can fix bugs faster later.

11
00:00:34.168 --> 00:00:35.690
Teams share code.

12
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.550
Let us recap.

13
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.459
Clarity is part of quality.

14
00:00:41.509 --> 00:00:45.444
Small cleanups prevent big confusion.

